ok - repair and replay do not wake firstmate for an already-acknowledged note
ok - receipts JSON is bounded by fixed bounds and discloses what it omitted
ok - notes that predate the announcement marker are unknown, not re-announced
ok - the reply channel is durable and its cursor is a strict order
ok - the reply cursor never goes backwards when the sequence counter is lost
ok - a reply without a valid sequence is reported as malformed
ok - a non-UTF-8 note does not break the receipts view
ok - the drain refuses to ack an unacked presented note and passes once it is acked
ok - every unacked note in the range is named, and an acked note is not
ok - an unacked note outside the acknowledged range does not block
ok - a range with no inbox note rows acks exactly as before
ok - an absent inbox fails closed, then an acked note lets the ack pass
ok - a wake naming an unknown note refuses until its ack is recorded; a handled note does not
ok - an unreadable inbox fails closed and the wake rows stay
ok - a failed queue scan refuses the ack and keeps the rows; an empty range still acks
